  <model metaid="meta_rivaroxaban_kidney" id="rivaroxaban_kidney" name="Model for renal rivaroxaban excretion." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for renal rivaroxaban excretion.</p>
        <p>The renal clearance of rivaroxaban is the filtration of its unbound
fraction, <code>GFR * fu_riv</code>, times <code>RIVEX_f</code> for the active secretion by P-gp
and BCRP (<code>f_pgp</code>); the glomerular filtration rate is the renal function
times the healthy GFR of 101 ml/min. About 36 % of an oral dose of 10 mg is
excreted unchanged in the urine (Weinz2009, Kubitza2013).</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
